author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: "Typed transport contracts exactly represent official current REST and WebSocket requests and responses; call-service supports normalized dry-run planning, explicit transport, target selectors, inline/file service data, response capability modes, and local validation; Read-only mode blocks executing action calls before network I/O on both transports but allows dry-run discovery; Actual built hassio passes setup wizard, recursive help, every formatter/schema, private live response action, 100 percent coverage/docstrings, static/security/PM/package/changelog, and non-publishing auto-release gates"
definition_of_ready: "Feature, plan, regression issue, official docs, live server capability counts, and previous related PM items are linked"
goal: agent-safe-home-assistant-actions
objective: implement-cross-transport-service-actions
value: Give agents one predictable action execution surface.
impact: "Improves API fidelity, safety, observability, and programmatic output stability."
outcome: Production-ready merged implementation without publishing.
why_now: Official and live response contracts expose a type and UX gap today.
parent: hac-stpm
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 94
sprint: api-parity-2026-07
release: unreleased
resolution: "Implemented and verified typed action contracts, stable transport-neutral envelopes, read-only planning, current TOON and full release gates."
expected_result: "One safe, typed, documented action surface with exact official transport behavior and complete production-readiness evidence."
actual_result: "REST and WebSocket execution, required-response discovery, selector targeting, file/inline inputs, dry-run, strict environment parsing, 100 percent gates and live acceptance pass."
